# Editor UI Conventions

These conventions apply to the embeddable editor shipped from `@catamorphic/ui` / `@catamorphic/react` / `@catamorphic/registry`. There is no standalone playground app — the host mounts the editor and wires data through its own API layer.

## Data access rule

Editor components **must only communicate with the embed server** (either `@catamorphic/fastify-plugin` mounted by the host, or via `@catamorphic/server-sdk`). They never import from `@catamorphic/db` or talk to the database directly. All data flows through `@catamorphic/api-client` or the host's own proxy.

## Run Execution Flow

1. User clicks **▶ Run** → `RunTriggerDialog` opens with a form built from `triggerParameters`.
2. On submit, a local pending run is added to `runsAtom` (status `running`).
3. The **History sidebar** opens automatically and the running run is expanded.
4. `onRun(triggerData)` fires the host-provided callback → `POST /api/projects/:projectId/workflows/:name/runs` on the embed server.
5. On completion, the local run is updated with the server's `runId`, result, and status.
6. If the server persisted the run to the DB, `runId` is the DB-assigned UUID (replaces the local temp ID).

## History Sidebar

- Opened by the **⏱ History** toolbar button (not a tab inside the right panel).
- Has two tabs: **Runs** and **Versions** (code history).
- The run count is **not** shown on the button.
- Closed by: clicking the button again, clicking ✕ inside the sidebar, or pressing **Escape** (Escape closes history sidebar first; pressing again closes the right detail panel).

## Runs Panel Behavior

- One Runs panel renders every Workflow. Run capabilities determine whether
  cancel, processing pause/resume, input submission, progress, and item
  inspection controls appear; never add capability-specific panel families.
- Runs start **collapsed by default** — DB-loaded history is never auto-expanded.
- Only the run triggered in the **current session** (`activeRunIdAtom`) auto-expands.
- Runs are paginated: 20 per page. An `IntersectionObserver` sentinel at the bottom triggers `onLoadMoreRuns(offset)` when scrolled into view, appending more items to `runsAtom`.

## State Management Rules

- `runsAtom` — plain Jotai atom, **in-memory only** (no sessionStorage, no localStorage). Seeded from DB on page load via `initialRuns` prop.
- `lastTriggerDataAtom` — plain Jotai atom, **in-memory only**. Remembers the last trigger data values to pre-fill the dialog on next run. Never persist to storage.
- `loadMoreRunsAtom` — holds the `onLoadMoreRuns` callback, set from `WorkflowEditorProps`. Allows `RunsPanel` to fetch additional pages without knowing the API URL.

## Canvas Interaction Rules

- Edge interaction paths (`react-flow__edge-interaction`) have `pointer-events: none` — dragging on an edge pans the canvas instead of initiating an edge interaction.
- The graph is read-only; users cannot drag, connect, or delete nodes or edges.

## Detail Panel (Right Panel)

- Shows **Details** and **Code** tabs.
- **Node count is not shown** on the workflow overview (trigger details). Only trigger parameters and description are shown.
- See `panel-editor.mdc` for full bidirectional code ↔ canvas linking conventions.
